00:11:23.770 --> 00:11:25.190
- But it's a very, I wanna stay on this,

00:11:25.190 --> 00:11:26.410
it's a very important point,

00:11:26.410 --> 00:11:27.960
this is what you signed up for.

00:11:29.070 --> 00:11:30.460
If you don't have the confidence,

00:11:30.460 --> 00:11:33.260
you can build it through
historical staying alive.

00:11:33.260 --> 00:11:35.350
Do you know how many people here...

00:11:35.350 --> 00:11:37.110
Clap up if you've had your own business

00:11:37.110 --> 00:11:38.380
for more than five years.

00:11:38.380 --> 00:11:41.547
(audience applauding)

00:11:42.870 --> 00:11:44.870
The level of admiration
I have for everybody

00:11:44.870 --> 00:11:46.620
who just clapped, it's hard.

00:11:46.620 --> 00:11:48.440
Your confidence should
come from the fact that

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:50.180
you're part of a small group of people

00:11:50.180 --> 00:11:52.840
that decided to take on
the risk to begin with.

00:11:52.840 --> 00:11:53.673
Anybody would just clap

00:11:53.673 --> 00:11:56.420
and has been doing it for
five years that's remarkable,

00:11:57.330 --> 00:11:58.730
but don't be audacious

00:11:58.730 --> 00:12:00.840
if somebody big comes along,

00:12:00.840 --> 00:12:02.330
they're better than you then,

00:12:02.330 --> 00:12:04.020
that's what you're saying.

00:12:04.020 --> 00:12:05.220
Don't cry about it,

00:12:05.220 --> 00:12:06.580
don't try to change the rules

00:12:06.580 --> 00:12:07.940
'cause it's not working for you.

00:12:07.940 --> 00:12:10.420
My favorite version of
it is you were small,

00:12:10.420 --> 00:12:12.060
you got bigger and hurt other people,

00:12:12.060 --> 00:12:14.320
but now somebody else came
along and is bigger than you,

00:12:14.320 --> 00:12:16.590
and you're crying about it, right?

00:12:16.590 --> 00:12:17.920
You weren't crying when you were taking

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.802
other people's money.

00:12:19.802 --> 00:12:21.564
So don't cry when I'll take yours.

00:12:21.564 --> 00:12:22.397
(audience laughing)

00:12:22.397 --> 00:12:23.350
- I love it.

00:12:23.350 --> 00:12:24.990
All right, this is from
Mark Sky on Twitter.

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:26.610
My girlfriend and I are
quitting our careers

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:29.250
to take on an ambitious
20,000 kilometer bike ride

00:12:29.250 --> 00:12:31.440
and paddle from home
in Canada to a summit,

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:34.810
as a charity adventure
that lasts 18 months.

00:12:34.810 --> 00:12:37.433
What is the best way to gain exposure?

00:12:42.200 --> 00:12:43.930
- The best way to gain exposure

00:12:43.930 --> 00:12:47.390
is to do the most obvious thing
to everybody in this room,

00:12:47.390 --> 00:12:49.400
anybody could sit in this
seat and answer this,

00:12:49.400 --> 00:12:51.760
which is to document the entire journey.

00:12:51.760 --> 00:12:55.030
The question is, are
you good enough at it?

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:56.510
Everybody knows the answer.

00:12:56.510 --> 00:12:58.370
You start a blog and
you put it on YouTube,

00:12:58.370 --> 00:12:59.690
you chop up all the pieces of content

00:12:59.690 --> 00:13:02.590
you put on TikTok and
Instagram and Twitter,

00:13:02.590 --> 00:13:03.823
but are they compelling?

00:13:04.930 --> 00:13:07.520
Do they know how to post that content?

00:13:07.520 --> 00:13:09.703
Will they reply to all the comments?

00:13:10.960 --> 00:13:14.020
People's lack of patience
with building exposure

00:13:14.020 --> 00:13:15.720
is why most people don't have any.

00:13:17.090 --> 00:13:18.740
It took me two years of Wine Library TV

00:13:18.740 --> 00:13:20.010
before anybody gave a shit.

00:13:20.010 --> 00:13:22.010
I did it five days a week for two years.

00:13:24.281 --> 00:13:27.730
(audience applauding)

00:13:27.730 --> 00:13:29.640
- Now, Gary, in one of your podcasts,

00:13:29.640 --> 00:13:30.950
you said something super commendable

00:13:30.950 --> 00:13:34.080
that you actually had a
position in your company

00:13:34.080 --> 00:13:35.570
for someone to read the comments,

00:13:35.570 --> 00:13:37.380
reply to people.

00:13:37.380 --> 00:13:38.213
And from there,

00:13:38.213 --> 00:13:39.920
you guys create this assessment

00:13:39.920 --> 00:13:42.270
as to what your content should be.

00:13:42.270 --> 00:13:43.310
Can we talk a little bit about

00:13:43.310 --> 00:13:45.220
the importance of replying to comments

00:13:45.220 --> 00:13:48.510
and acknowledging people in social media.

00:13:48.510 --> 00:13:50.611
- Like in the prior
session, to your point,

00:13:50.611 --> 00:13:55.000
we have a very prominent role
at VaynerMedia called PCS,

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.160
post creative strategist.

00:13:57.160 --> 00:14:00.840
These individuals' jobs
are to read every comment

00:14:00.840 --> 00:14:03.610
from every post of a brand

00:14:03.610 --> 00:14:08.043
and then use their psychology,
anthropology skills

00:14:09.140 --> 00:14:11.630
to make observations from the comments,

00:14:11.630 --> 00:14:14.870
by reading the qualitative data

00:14:14.870 --> 00:14:16.260
and inform an insight

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:18.110
that makes the next piece of content.

00:14:19.290 --> 00:14:21.750
The amount of people
that hit me up every day

00:14:21.750 --> 00:14:25.890
is hundreds, thousands
of people who are sad

00:14:25.890 --> 00:14:27.340
that they're not growing.

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:28.970
And then occasionally,

00:14:28.970 --> 00:14:29.920
I used to do it all the time,

00:14:29.920 --> 00:14:31.290
now I do it occasionally

00:14:31.290 --> 00:14:33.010
I will go look at their account.

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:35.470
90% of those people don't even reply

00:14:35.470 --> 00:14:37.540
to the 15 people that leave a comment.

00:14:37.540 --> 00:14:38.860
If you're in this audience,

00:14:38.860 --> 00:14:40.760
and you're sad that your
profile is not growing

00:14:40.760 --> 00:14:42.480
on the business side or the personal side,

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.160
and you are not replying
to every comment you get

00:14:45.160 --> 00:14:47.310
from the content you are putting out,

00:14:47.310 --> 00:14:48.593
you are audacious.

00:14:50.100 --> 00:14:51.064
Thank you.

00:14:51.064 --> 00:14:53.460
(audience laughing)

00:14:53.460 --> 00:14:55.520
- I love this next question
from Michael on Twitter.

00:14:55.520 --> 00:14:57.300
He asks, what are the key principles

00:14:57.300 --> 00:14:59.213
to happiness and success in life?

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:07.157
- I believe it's simplicity, I really do.

00:15:07.157 --> 00:15:11.170
I think for the people
that know me in my life,

00:15:11.170 --> 00:15:13.290
I'm really simple.

00:15:13.290 --> 00:15:15.660
I really enjoy my career, I love this.

00:15:15.660 --> 00:15:19.100
Like you couldn't even
imagine how humbled I am

00:15:19.100 --> 00:15:22.190
by people's interest in what I talk about,

00:15:22.190 --> 00:15:25.210
but I think the key to happiness

00:15:25.210 --> 00:15:28.320
is being content while being ambitious.

00:15:28.320 --> 00:15:31.350
And I think being content
comes from gratitude.

00:15:31.350 --> 00:15:33.090
I'm so grateful for what I have,

00:15:33.090 --> 00:15:34.630
and I've always been that way,

00:15:34.630 --> 00:15:37.640
that all this special stuff
that has been happening

00:15:37.640 --> 00:15:39.700
doesn't mean enough to me.

00:15:39.700 --> 00:15:42.140
This is not where my self worth comes in.

00:15:42.140 --> 00:15:44.110
The Gary Vee crap and the
collapse and the follower,

00:15:44.110 --> 00:15:45.760
like it's incredible,

00:15:45.760 --> 00:15:49.540
but it's not what I aspire to,

00:15:49.540 --> 00:15:52.160
it's not how I see my value.

00:15:52.160 --> 00:15:55.930
And I think the only way to be happy

00:15:55.930 --> 00:15:57.820
is to have a quiet mind.

00:15:57.820 --> 00:16:00.270
And I think a quiet mind comes from

00:16:00.270 --> 00:16:03.130
a balance of very deep humility

00:16:03.130 --> 00:16:06.510
and true perspective of understanding that

00:16:06.510 --> 00:16:08.270
like you just genuinely understand

00:16:08.270 --> 00:16:11.200
that you don't mean shit
in the scheme of things,

00:16:11.200 --> 00:16:14.820
but you aspire in your
behavior to mean something.

00:16:14.820 --> 00:16:16.500
And I think it's a very
interesting balance

00:16:16.500 --> 00:16:18.830
that I think it works incredibly well.

00:16:18.830 --> 00:16:20.193
I just wish people,

00:16:21.420 --> 00:16:24.160
people are just impossibly addicted

00:16:24.160 --> 00:16:27.420
to outside affirmation, to acceptance.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:30.190
And I wish people lived
in their own cocoon

00:16:30.190 --> 00:16:32.320
and just did the things
that made them happy.

00:16:32.320 --> 00:16:33.280
So many people

00:16:34.270 --> 00:16:36.670
would aspire to make so much less money

00:16:36.670 --> 00:16:38.260
if they didn't care about
what other people think

00:16:38.260 --> 00:16:40.220
and would be dramatically happier,

00:16:40.220 --> 00:16:41.830
dramatically happier.

00:16:41.830 --> 00:16:43.570
And I wish that in society.

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:44.700
- Now, what do you do when...

00:16:44.700 --> 00:16:47.464
Yeah, it's gone, they're all good ones.

00:16:47.464 --> 00:16:48.297
(audience applauding)

00:16:48.297 --> 00:16:50.230
- It's a tough conversation because

00:16:50.230 --> 00:16:51.260
in the business world,

00:16:51.260 --> 00:16:52.950
so many people think that scoring

00:16:52.950 --> 00:16:54.580
is based on how big your net worth is

00:16:54.580 --> 00:16:55.940
or how much money you make.

00:16:55.940 --> 00:16:57.390
And it's really unfortunate

00:16:57.390 --> 00:16:59.880
'cause I think troop red entrepreneurship

00:16:59.880 --> 00:17:01.180
almost doesn't give a shit about

00:17:01.180 --> 00:17:02.960
all the collateral that
comes along with it,

00:17:02.960 --> 00:17:05.750
it's art, you just love doing it.

00:17:05.750 --> 00:17:07.720
And we've got to find our balance

00:17:07.720 --> 00:17:09.800
much like the chat I had upfront

00:17:09.800 --> 00:17:12.340
as I spend the next half decade refining

00:17:12.340 --> 00:17:13.580
what I talked to you about up there,

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:15.030
and what I'm talking about right now is

00:17:15.030 --> 00:17:19.040
we have to change the
definition of success.

00:17:19.040 --> 00:17:21.880
We have to, it cannot be the flex.

00:17:21.880 --> 00:17:26.250
We can not put expensive watches and cars

00:17:26.250 --> 00:17:27.870
and bank accounts on a pedestal,

00:17:27.870 --> 00:17:29.950
we must get away from that.

00:17:29.950 --> 00:17:32.880
But that doesn't mean
we demonize it either.

00:17:32.880 --> 00:17:35.448
We have to make it about
the process of the game.

00:17:35.448 --> 00:17:36.820
We've gotta find our way

00:17:36.820 --> 00:17:38.200
'cause right now we're over here.

00:17:38.200 --> 00:17:40.240
We've got to find this.

00:17:40.240 --> 00:17:42.030
- Now, Gary, tell me when life hits,

00:17:42.030 --> 00:17:43.140
when the storm of life hits,

00:17:43.140 --> 00:17:44.080
'cause we've all been there,

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:44.930
no matter who you are,

00:17:44.930 --> 00:17:46.830
how do you remain in that state

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:49.363
and that space of gratitude and balance.

00:17:50.570 --> 00:17:51.430
- Very easily.

00:17:51.430 --> 00:17:54.220
When your entire life
has only predicated on

00:17:54.220 --> 00:17:55.380
the health and wellbeing

00:17:55.380 --> 00:17:56.510
of a small group of people

00:17:56.510 --> 00:17:58.310
you love more than breathing,

00:17:58.310 --> 00:17:59.323
nothing scares you.

00:18:01.682 --> 00:18:04.700
(audience applauding)

00:18:04.700 --> 00:18:06.770
I mean, the first couple
of months of COVID,

00:18:06.770 --> 00:18:08.900
Vayner was a very weird spot.

00:18:08.900 --> 00:18:10.080
I don't build it for profits,

00:18:10.080 --> 00:18:12.130
so we didn't have profit.

00:18:12.130 --> 00:18:13.770
You know, I built it for growth.

00:18:13.770 --> 00:18:14.810
We were very weird,

00:18:14.810 --> 00:18:17.190
in the US the way they
subsidized businesses,

00:18:17.190 --> 00:18:18.023
we were in the middle,

00:18:18.023 --> 00:18:20.070
we weren't small enough
and weren't big enough,

00:18:20.070 --> 00:18:21.640
so we got nothing.

00:18:21.640 --> 00:18:23.770
All of our clients are humongous

00:18:23.770 --> 00:18:25.370
and all of them right away said,

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:28.130
we're gonna slow down the way we pay you.

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:29.500
It was a very big challenge,

00:18:29.500 --> 00:18:33.070
and I just remember having the
greatest moment with myself

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:36.630
when it was super scary
week one saying, oh my God,

00:18:36.630 --> 00:18:38.620
everything I've been telling them is true.

00:18:38.620 --> 00:18:41.170
If this company goes out of business,

00:18:41.170 --> 00:18:42.863
I'll be beyond okay.

00:18:44.570 --> 00:18:45.960
- I love that, I have a question because

00:18:45.960 --> 00:18:47.400
what you said prior to what you just said,

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:49.140
really hit home for me
because in my previous role,

00:18:49.140 --> 00:18:50.490
in my previous job,

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:54.340
I actually attached my
worth and my identity to

00:18:54.340 --> 00:18:56.840
income, my job, my work,

00:18:56.840 --> 00:18:58.600
my schedule, social media,

00:18:58.600 --> 00:18:59.980
because I worked so hard to get it.

00:18:59.980 --> 00:19:01.320
I fell in kind of that loophole

00:19:01.320 --> 00:19:04.700
then life hit me with a
very big wake up call.

00:19:04.700 --> 00:19:07.530
And I was stuck with this
super uncomfortable feeling

00:19:07.530 --> 00:19:10.420
of my internal changing,

00:19:10.420 --> 00:19:12.400
and if I didn't change my external,

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:13.450
it just wasn't working

00:19:13.450 --> 00:19:15.500
and I became a very unhappy person.

00:19:15.500 --> 00:19:17.830
So just in case there's
anyone in the crowd

00:19:17.830 --> 00:19:19.100
and the fans and the audience,

00:19:19.100 --> 00:19:20.890
anyone listening online who can relate,

00:19:20.890 --> 00:19:22.110
what would be your advice to them

00:19:22.110 --> 00:19:23.140
to have that courage,

00:19:23.140 --> 00:19:26.610
to start redefining success in their life.

00:19:26.610 --> 00:19:27.873
- That they can.

00:19:29.070 --> 00:19:30.980
Like everybody's so obsessed

00:19:30.980 --> 00:19:33.510
on what they've done and said.

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:35.320
Like the greatest gift in the world

00:19:35.320 --> 00:19:38.070
is the ability to be comfortable
in changing your mind.

00:19:40.493 --> 00:19:43.170
(audience applauding)

00:19:43.170 --> 00:19:47.250
Actually, I have a very
different thing to say right now.

00:19:47.250 --> 00:19:50.450
We need to start hanging
out with 90 year olds more.

00:19:50.450 --> 00:19:51.283
(audience laughing)

00:19:51.283 --> 00:19:52.116
I mean this.

00:19:53.291 --> 00:19:56.440
You wanna do something that will bring you

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:58.230
an incredible amount of value,

00:19:58.230 --> 00:19:59.770
but also bring someone else

00:19:59.770 --> 00:20:01.720
an incredible amount of value,

00:20:01.720 --> 00:20:05.563
go donate your time to a
retirement home for one week,

00:20:06.410 --> 00:20:09.550
you will learn a lesson real fast

00:20:09.550 --> 00:20:11.700
that 99% of the stuff that all of you

00:20:11.700 --> 00:20:14.513
are right now thinking
about means jack shit.

00:20:16.210 --> 00:20:17.853
This is a game of perspective.

00:20:18.800 --> 00:20:21.153
I don't understand how
we don't understand that.

00:20:22.090 --> 00:20:25.580
You must shift perspective
into simplicity,

00:20:25.580 --> 00:20:28.160
which then makes the
ability to do what we all do

00:20:28.160 --> 00:20:29.720
so much more palpable

00:20:29.720 --> 00:20:31.690
because there's no weight on it,

00:20:31.690 --> 00:20:33.330
because it doesn't matter as much,

00:20:33.330 --> 00:20:36.220
which then inherently
makes it more enjoyable.

00:20:36.220 --> 00:20:38.210
Of course, you're gonna burn out

00:20:38.210 --> 00:20:39.680
if your entire self worth

00:20:39.680 --> 00:20:42.210
is in how good your business is doing.

00:20:42.210 --> 00:20:44.400
Of course, you're gonna burn out.

00:20:44.400 --> 00:20:45.500
A funny thing happens

00:20:45.500 --> 00:20:47.850
you don't burn out from games.

00:20:47.850 --> 00:20:49.680
When you make your career a game

00:20:50.690 --> 00:20:52.550
things changed very quickly.

00:20:52.550 --> 00:20:53.530
- I love that,

00:20:53.530 --> 00:20:54.878
I'm gonna start the clap on that one.

00:20:54.878 --> 00:20:56.447
(audience applauding)

00:20:56.447 --> 00:20:58.390
All right, next, we have a video question

00:20:58.390 --> 00:21:00.493
from a Facebook winner, Matt Huber.

00:21:01.430 --> 00:21:03.940
- Gary Vee, it's Matt
huber here in Edmonton.

00:21:03.940 --> 00:21:05.550
Absolutely love what you do.

00:21:05.550 --> 00:21:07.970
The focus big time on the humility aspect.

00:21:07.970 --> 00:21:10.660
We're five-year stronger on
20 to 30% year over year,

00:21:10.660 --> 00:21:12.570
we got 20 Albertans working with us

00:21:12.570 --> 00:21:13.790
and just rocking it.

00:21:13.790 --> 00:21:14.810
Our question for you is

00:21:14.810 --> 00:21:16.030
how do we get from the small business

00:21:16.030 --> 00:21:17.450
to the medium sized business?

00:21:17.450 --> 00:21:19.840
We got managers and we're
helping them succeed,

00:21:19.840 --> 00:21:20.710
but how do we let go?

00:21:20.710 --> 00:21:22.610
How do we grow that to the next level?

00:21:24.570 --> 00:21:26.120
- What's tough about video questions is

00:21:26.120 --> 00:21:27.210
you wanna ask them,

00:21:27.210 --> 00:21:28.550
you know, there's the next question there.

00:21:28.550 --> 00:21:30.810
It's like, you know, again,

00:21:30.810 --> 00:21:33.080
I talk about these, the Maddix a lot,

00:21:33.080 --> 00:21:35.330
and I will repeat them to my death.

00:21:35.330 --> 00:21:37.610
The best way to go from a small business

00:21:37.610 --> 00:21:39.350
to a medium business

00:21:39.350 --> 00:21:40.720
is by deploying patience

00:21:40.720 --> 00:21:42.320
and doing what you did

00:21:42.320 --> 00:21:44.390
to get to become a small business.

00:21:44.390 --> 00:21:45.940
Of course there are strategies.

00:21:45.940 --> 00:21:47.520
I've been very consistent about this.

00:21:47.520 --> 00:21:50.240
For 15 years, I put out
a very simple message

00:21:50.240 --> 00:21:52.770
that has been uncomfortably
historically true.

00:21:52.770 --> 00:21:55.290
If you understand where the
customer's attention is,

00:21:55.290 --> 00:21:57.830
and you know how to make pictures,
videos, and written words

00:21:57.830 --> 00:22:00.180
for those platforms, you will grow.

00:22:00.180 --> 00:22:01.310
For that gentleman's business,

00:22:01.310 --> 00:22:03.710
if he got great at LinkedIn ads,

00:22:03.710 --> 00:22:05.810
his top line revenue would grow.

00:22:05.810 --> 00:22:08.330
The question is, how's he judging himself?

00:22:08.330 --> 00:22:11.470
By the way, what is even a
small or medium business?

00:22:11.470 --> 00:22:13.000
Like what are the rules of all that shit?

00:22:13.000 --> 00:22:14.940
Is like, is 5 million small?

00:22:14.940 --> 00:22:16.360
Is 50 million medium?

00:22:16.360 --> 00:22:18.070
Like, what is this shit?

00:22:18.070 --> 00:22:20.120
